+  "home.294": "How long until a worker actually starts?",
+  "home.295": "About 45 days on average from signed contract to work-permit approval, plus 1–2 weeks for travel and arrival. Urgent seasonal cases can move faster — we give you the real timeline before you sign.",
+  "home.296": "Do we have to handle any paperwork?",
+  "home.297": "No. We file and track every application under law No. 4904 — permit, contract, SGK registration and arrival formalities. Your side is three steps: share the requirement, approve the shortlist, sign the contract.",
+  "home.298": "What does a worker really cost per month?",
+  "home.299": "At 2026 minimum wage roughly ₺38,944 per worker per month including SGK and the standard discount, plus one-time permit and flight costs. Skilled roles carry a higher legal salary floor — the calculator on this site shows your exact case.",
+  "home.300": "What if a worker leaves or doesn't fit?",
+  "home.301": "Every candidate is interviewed and document-checked by our own representative before you see the profile. If a placement fails in the agreed guarantee period, we replace the worker — the terms are written into your contract, not promised verbally.",
+  "home.302": "Does the worker pay any fee?",
+  "home.303": "Never. Job seekers are never charged a fee (law No. 4904). Anyone asking a worker for money is not working for us — check their JA- ID on the public register and report them to us.",
