+  "hire.283": "Weeks 2–6",
+  "hire.284": "Work permits processed",
+  "hire.285": "We file every permit and track it to approval — you follow live status on your dashboard.",
+  "hire.286": "Weeks 6–8",
+  "hire.287": "Arrival & first day",
+  "hire.288": "Visa, travel and onboarding coordinated by us. Workers arrive ready to start — with follow-up support after.",
+  "hire.289": "What is my responsibility as the employer?",
+  "hire.290": "You provide the job, the salary and the workplace. Accommodation and transport are agreed case by case and written into the contract before we start — many employers provide housing, others pay an allowance. We handle sourcing, permits, contracts and the arrival process.",
+  "hire.291": "What does it cost?",
+  "hire.292": "Pricing depends on roles, headcount and source country, so we prepare a custom quote for every requirement. Sourcing and interviews are free — you pay one agreed fee per placed worker, invoiced after arrival. Written proposal within 24 hours, no obligation.",
+  "hire.293": "Is there a minimum number of workers?",
+  "hire.294": "No. We place single specialists as well as full teams of 50+. Smaller requests simply move faster, because fewer permit files are processed in parallel.",
+  "hire.295": "What happens if a work permit is rejected?",
+  "hire.296": "Rejections are rare because we pre-check every file, but if one happens we re-file at our own cost or replace the candidate — you are not charged a placement fee for a worker who never arrives. Official state fees already paid are shown with receipts.",
+  "hire.297": "How do you verify skills before we interview?",
+  "hire.298": "Every candidate goes through document checks, reference calls and a trade test or practical assessment for skilled roles. You then run your own video interview through the portal before approving anyone — you always make the final choice.",
+  "hire.299": "Will workers understand instructions on site?",
+  "hire.300": "Candidates are screened for language level and it is shown on every profile. For production and construction roles we prioritise workers with basic Turkish — English is assessed for tourism and hospitality roles — and teams are usually placed with an experienced lead worker who translates on site.",
+  "hire.301": "What if a worker leaves or doesn't perform?",
