+  "calc.202": "About ₺16,000 in state fees, once",
+  "calc.203": "+ the flight — paid one time, for years of work",
+  "calc.204": "Who accepts the wage",
+  "calc.205": "At minimum wage, most local applicants keep looking. For the same money they can work in a shop or café in the city centre.",
+  "calc.206": "The same registered wage fills the job",
+  "calc.207": "— people apply for it, and for them this is a real career step, not a short-term job",
+  "calc.208": "Where the work is",
+  "calc.209": "Factories in small cities and industrial zones have the hardest time. Young people move to the big cities and do not return for factory shifts.",
+  "calc.210": "Workers move to where the factory is",
+  "calc.211": "— a small city, a farm or a remote site is not a problem for these candidates",
+  "calc.212": "Availability",
+  "calc.213": "Hard for skilled trades — welders, machine operators and seasonal jobs often stay empty for months",
+  "calc.214": "Checked candidates, ready now",
+  "calc.215": "— their skills are tested before you interview them",
+  "calc.216": "Retention",
+  "calc.217": "People leave often in low-wage jobs, so you hire and train again and again",
+  "calc.218": "The permit is",
+  "calc.219": "tied to your workplace",
+  "calc.220": ", so the worker stays with you for the contract",
