+  "wp.135": "Ongoing job on your payroll? This is your route.",
+  "wp.136": "Short, one-off assignment? Check the categories below.",
+  "wp.137": "Important:",
+  "wp.138": "if the work will run past the exemption period, a full work permit is mandatory from the start — and the same exemption category cannot be re-used for 6–12 months after it ends. For ongoing employment, the standard permit is the only legal route.",
+  "wp.139": "Sample document",
+  "wp.140": "What the work permit card looks like",
+  "wp.141": "A credit-card-sized document issued by the Ministry of Labour and Social Security — it carries the worker's photo, the employer, the validity dates and a foreigner ID number starting with 99. This card is what the worker shows at the airport, the bank and SGK.",
