+  "wp.187": "Rules & regulations",
+  "wp.188": "What the Ministry checks before approving",
+  "wp.189": "Most rejections are not about missing documents — they are about employer criteria. These are the rules under Law No. 6735 and its implementing regulation, checked on every application. When you",
+  "wp.190": "hire through us",
+  "wp.191": ", we pre-check all of them before anything is filed.",
+  "wp.192": "Most rejections are not about documents — they are about",
+  "wp.193": "employer criteria",
+  "wp.194": ". We pre-check all six before filing.",
+  "wp.195": "Working without a permit costs",
+  "wp.196": "· Administrative fine per unauthorised worker — over ₺100,000 in 2026, updated every year",
+  "wp.197": "· Deportation and entry ban for the worker — at the employer's expense",
+  "wp.198": "· Block on the employer's future work permit applications",
+  "wp.199": "· Possible criminal liability for company directors",
+  "wp.200": "The 1:5 employment ratio",
+  "wp.201": "At least five Turkish citizens on SGK payroll for each foreign worker, per workplace. Monitored monthly from the 7th month of the first permit — so a new employer has time to build up.",
+  "wp.202": "Financial capacity",
+  "wp.203": "The company must show paid-in capital or gross sales above the Ministry's thresholds — proof that the business can genuinely carry a foreign employee.",
+  "wp.204": "Role-based salary thresholds",
+  "wp.205": "Each role has a minimum gross salary set as a multiple of the Turkish minimum wage — higher for specialists and managers. Updated every January; underpaying is an automatic rejection.",
+  "wp.206": "No tax or SGK debts",
+  "wp.207": "Overdue tax or social security premiums suspend the application. Ministry, SGK and Revenue Administration databases are linked — discrepancies are flagged instantly.",
+  "wp.208": "SGK registration from day one",
+  "wp.209": "Once the permit is approved, the worker must be registered with social security immediately and paid the declared salary through the books.",
+  "wp.210": "Sector-specific rules",
+  "wp.211": "Health roles need Ministry of Health pre-authorisation; tourism and advanced-technology investments enjoy exemptions from some employment criteria; public projects are exempt from financial criteria.",
+  "wp.212": "Who qualifies for the work permit exemption",
+  "wp.213": "Article 48 of the implementing regulation lists exact categories. If the assignment fits one, the foreigner applies online — no employer criteria, no 1:5 ratio.",
+  "wp.214": "For the standard permit, eligibility depends on the employer instead — see",
