+  "wp.332": "WhatsApp",
+  "wp.333": "Email",
+  "wp.334": "How long does a Turkish work permit take?",
+  "wp.335": "Around 30 days of Ministry processing once the file is complete. If the worker is abroad, add the consular work visa stage before that. With our pre-check, most files pass on the first submission — rejected files that need re-filing take far longer, which is why the pre-check matters.",
+  "wp.336": "Does the worker also need a residence permit?",
+  "wp.337": "No. Under Law No. 6735, a valid work permit counts as a residence permit for its whole validity. The worker can live in Turkey and re-enter the country on the permit alone.",
+  "wp.338": "What exactly is the 1:5 rule?",
+  "wp.339": "For each foreign worker, the workplace must employ at least five Turkish citizens registered with SGK. It is monitored monthly starting from the 7th month of the first permit, so new employers have a build-up window. Some sectors and situations are exempt — tourism specialists, advanced-technology investments and public projects among them.",
+  "wp.340": "What is e-Muafiyet and who can use it?",
+  "wp.341": "What happens if someone works without a permit?",
+  "wp.342": "Administrative fines of over ₺100,000 per unauthorised worker in 2026 (updated every year), deportation of the worker at the employer's expense, a block on the employer's future applications, and possible criminal liability for directors. It is never worth it.",
+  "wp.343": "Is there a minimum salary for foreign workers?",
+  "wp.344": "Yes — each role has a minimum gross salary defined as a multiple of the Turkish minimum wage, higher for specialists and managers. The multiples are updated every January, and offering less is an automatic rejection.",
+  "wp.345": "We are a recruitment agency — can you file permits for our clients' workers?",
+  "wp.346": "Yes — that is exactly our HR agency partnership: you keep the client, we supply verified workers and file every permit under our İŞKUR licence. See the Partner With Us page for how the cooperation works, or message us on WhatsApp.",
+  "wp.347": "We already have a worker — can you handle just the permit?",
+  "wp.348": "Yes. Permit-only files are a normal part of our work: you bring the employee, we run the pre-check, the consular stage if needed, the Ministry filing and SGK registration under our İŞKUR licence. You don't have to hire through us to use our permit service.",
+  "wp.349": "Who files the permit when we hire through JobsAdmire?",
+  "wp.350": "We do — every stage, under our İŞKUR licence (Permit No. 1730): the company pre-check, the consular stage, the Ministry filing and SGK registration. You track the status live on your portal, and if a permit is rejected we re-file at our own cost.",
+  "wp.351": "Keep reading on the blog",
+  "wp.352": "All articles →",
+  "wp.353": "Turkey work permit rejection reasons — and how to avoid them",
+  "wp.354": "The 7 most common rejection causes, and the pre-checks that prevent them.",
+  "wp.355": "Work visa vs work permit in Turkey: what's the difference?",
+  "wp.356": "Two documents, two processes — and why workers abroad need both.",
+  "wp.357": "Work permit renewals: don't lose your workforce to missed deadlines",
+  "wp.358": "Renewal windows, required documents and how we track expiry dates.",
+  "wp.359": "With workers or without — we handle every permit",
