+  "jt.244": "Portfolio matters more than a diploma",
+  "jt.245": "Do you hire workers for jobs in Turkey through this page?",
+  "jt.246": "No. This page is only for roles inside JobsAdmire — our Antalya office team and our overseas representatives. Worker placement in Turkey is handled with our verified partner agencies abroad, not by direct application. We never ask a worker for money.",
+  "jt.247": "What does an overseas representative actually do?",
+  "jt.248": "You are our person in a source country. You meet partner agencies and institutes, check candidate documents, run first interviews and prepare people for the job they are going to. Everything you do is recorded in our system, so Antalya sees the same picture you do.",
+  "jt.249": "Can I work with you part-time or on a project basis?",
+  "jt.250": "Yes. Overseas roles come as full-time, part-time or project-based. Project work is tied to something specific — a trade test, a batch of documents, one recruitment day — with the scope, timeline and fee written before you start.",
+  "jt.251": "Do I need recruitment experience?",
+  "jt.252": "For Antalya office roles we prefer experience in HR, recruitment, permits or B2B sales, but we do hire junior people and train them. For overseas roles your local network and language matter more than a recruitment job title.",
+  "jt.253": "Which languages do you need?",
+  "jt.254": "Turkish and English are the working languages in Antalya. For overseas roles the local language plus workable English is enough — Turkish is a plus, never a requirement. We are especially short on Russian, Uzbek, Arabic and French.",
+  "jt.255": "How long does the hiring process take?",
+  "jt.256": "Around two to three weeks. You apply, confirm on WhatsApp, the system books your interview slot, our Admira AI assistant runs the first interview, our team reviews it, and then you have a video call with the manager. After the offer comes training and your certificate, and then you start.",
+  "jt.257": "What is the AI interview and is a human involved?",
+  "jt.258": "Our Admira AI assistant runs the first interview so that everyone gets the same questions and a fair, quick answer — in your own language, at a time you choose. It only scores and summarises. Every decision is made by our team, and the final interview is always with a real manager.",
+  "jt.259": "Do you provide training?",
+  "jt.260": "Yes, and it is part of the job. You go through our modules on Turkish work permit rules, ethical recruitment and our CRM. Completed modules are certified inside the system and stay on your record — useful to you even outside JobsAdmire.",
+  "jt.261": "Antalya office",
+  "jt.262": "Overseas",
+  "jt.263": "You apply",
+  "jt.264": "Portal or the short form below. A few minutes, and you get a reference number straight away.",
+  "jt.265": "Day 0",
+  "jt.266": "Confirm on WhatsApp",
+  "jt.267": "A message arrives on your WhatsApp. You reply to confirm it is really you and that you still want the role.",
+  "jt.268": "Same day",
+  "jt.269": "Your slot is booked automatically",
+  "jt.270": "Once you confirm, the system offers you interview times and books the one you pick. No waiting for someone to email you.",
+  "jt.271": "Within 24h",
+  "jt.272": "Interview with Admira AI",
+  "jt.273": "Our assistant runs the first interview in your own language, asks role-specific questions and scores the answers the same way for everybody.",
+  "jt.274": "Day 2–3",
+  "jt.275": "Our team reviews the result",
+  "jt.276": "A real person reads the transcript and the score, not just the number. This is where we decide who goes to the next stage.",
+  "jt.277": "2–3 days",
+  "jt.278": "Human interview",
+  "jt.279": "A video call with the manager of that desk — the work itself, your market, your questions. Then a written offer.",
+  "jt.280": "Week 2",
+  "jt.281": "Training, certificate, start",
+  "jt.282": "Work permit rules, ethical recruitment and our tools. You finish the modules, the certificate is issued in the system, and you start.",
+  "jt.283": "Week 3",
